;; spec:   stdlib §2.5 (a bulk vec builds the trie in one pass), §8.1 item 5 (count cases)
;; expect: accept
;; result: 260
;; audit:  clean
;; allocs: <= 30
;; roots:  ../../lib support
;; covers: vec
;; vec of an Array of 260 elements, the walk's default to-vec: 8 full leaves and 4 elements in the buffer.
;; The leaves array has doubled once (4 slots to 8, at the 5th leaf) and the 8 leaves fill it, so the
;; root branch is that array itself and not a copy of it. A leaves array that grows by more than a
;; doubling (4 slots to 16) is not full when the walk ends and is copied (1 more object: 31); every
;; element still reads right, so only the count shows it. The mutation review (MUT-L9) found `(shl k 1)`
;; to `(shl k 2)` in the doubling surviving every case before this one. 30 is measured; the harness's
;; own test lowers the bound by one and requires the failure.
(ns main (:use fib.core fib.seq fib.coll))

(defun main () -> i64
  (let ((v (vec (array 260 0))))
    (count v)))
